Ah, I apologize - I can't directly upload image files through this interface. However, I can help you in a few ways:

**Option 1: Push via Git (Recommended)**
1. Download the image file from the chat
2. Place it in your local repository folder as `ella-portrait.jpg`
3. Run these commands:
   ```bash
   git add ella-portrait.jpg
   git commit -m "Add profile photo"
   git push origin main
   ```

**Option 2: GitHub Web Upload**
1. Go to https://github.com/efreund05/ellafweb
2. Click "Add file" → "Upload files"
3. Drag and drop or select the image
4. Name it `ella-portrait.jpg`
5. Commit the change

Your `index.html` is already configured to display the image at line 37 with `src="ella-portrait.jpg"`, so once you upload it, it will automatically appear in the hero section of your website!

Which method would you prefer?
